====================================================================================================
2. What is structural
====================================================================================================
  (a) 36 and 8 are even, 6 is even: Dropping Set_1, density 1/2.  17, 37, 9 are 1 mod 4: Set_3, density 1/4.
      35 = 3 mod 16: Set_6 (Terras k=4, s=2), density 1/16.  None of these classes is rare.
  (b) orbit(36) = [36, 18] + orbit(9), because 36 = 4*9.  The 3-smooth number 2^a 3^b simply halves a
      times and then follows 3^b.
  (c) v = n+1 = 2^a 3^b  =>  n makes exactly a odd shortcut steps (v -> 3v/2) and lands on 3^(a+b) - 1.
      v = 2^4 3^0 =  16   n =  15:  4 odd steps, then n = 80 = 3^4 - 1,  v2(3^4 - 1) = 4
      v = 2^3 3^1 =  24   n =  23:  3 odd steps, then n = 80 = 3^4 - 1,  v2(3^4 - 1) = 4
      v = 2^2 3^2 =  36   n =  35:  2 odd steps, then n = 80 = 3^4 - 1,  v2(3^4 - 1) = 4
      v = 2^1 3^3 =  54   n =  53:  1 odd steps, then n = 80 = 3^4 - 1,  v2(3^4 - 1) = 4
      v = 2^0 3^4 =  81   n =  80:  0 odd steps, then n = 80 = 3^4 - 1,  v2(3^4 - 1) = 4
      35 is the third point of the orbit of 15 = 2^4 - 1:  15 -> 23 -> 35 -> 53 -> 80 -> 40 -> 20 -> 10 -> 5.
      The whole anti-diagonal a+b = 4 shares the exit 80 = 3^4 - 1 = 2^4 * 5.

====================================================================================================
3. What is nothing (checked against base rates)
====================================================================================================
  orbit(36) passes through 17 and 8 (the u and the index of T_8 = 36).  Base rate for 1 <= n <= 1000:
     8 on the orbit: 997 (0.997);  17 on the orbit: 437 (0.437);  both: 437 (0.437).  Every orbit through 17 passes 8.
  total stopping time of 36 is 21 un-shortcut steps; for 2..100 the median is 19, min 1, max 118 (at 97).  Unremarkable.
  dropping genus of 36 = (1, 0, 17): index 17 because 36 is the 18th even number.  The '17' is 36/2 - 1.
  T_n along the -17 cycle contains T_(-37) = T_36 = 666; no content.
  T_(n0) at the cycle minima -5, -17 equals 10 = T_4, 136 = T_16, and -10, -136 lie on those cycles.
  With n0 = -(2^j + 1): T_(n0) = 2^(j-1) |n0|, and the cycle contains 2^i n0 for i up to the length e of
  its last halving run, so this says e >= j - 1.  Here (j, e) = (2, 1) and (4, 3): two instances, no mechanism.
